export anchor ColourGradeSuiteStyle:
    number: 355
    screen: VideoEditor
    name: Colour grade suite
    idea: A neutral eighteen percent grey grading room where scopes flank the picture, the inspector becomes a row of round wheels, and the bin is a strip of numbered thumbnails above a thin graticule timeline.
    base: dark
    palette:
        roomGrey: #1f1f1f, page and style sheet, kept neutral so colour judgement stays true
        panel: #2a2a2a, scope, viewer and wheel panels
        well: #242424, wheel wells and thumbnail cards
        scopeBlack: #121212, scope screens and the picture surround
        graticule: #4c4c4c, scope grid, wheel rims and lane edges
        ink: #e2e2e2, text
        muted: #ababab, labels, units and notes
        puck: #f0f0f0, wheel pucks, lit ticks, playhead and vectorscope dot
        trace: #bff0b4, the waveform luma trace
        neutralButton: #d4d4d4, Export, play and the selected clip, never a hue
        focusAmber: #f2b33d, focus outline and the marker, the one warm note
    type:
        One system sans stack for interface text and a mono stack for
        numbers. Base 13px at 1.45. Panel heads 11px at 600 in caps tracked
        0.14em with a lighter aside. The timecode is mono 17px at 500, wheel
        values mono 16px, graticule and ruler mono 9px to 10px. The title
        card uses a serif stack, Iowan Old Style, Palatino, Georgia, at up
        to 26px.
    layout:
        A slim header holds a small round hue wheel mark, Brightwork Cut, a
        slash, Launch teaser, a mono pill reading 1080p and 24 fps, then a
        thin render bar with Render 0% and a dashed box saying idle, and a
        light grey Export button. The suite is a three column grid. The left
        panel is a waveform scope on black with a 0 to 100 graticule and a
        pale green trace, low along the floor with a cluster near 90 in the
        middle third. The centre is the viewer with a 6px grey surround,
        then the timecode, three round transport buttons with a light grey
        play, and of plus the duration. The right panel is a vectorscope
        with two rings, crosshairs and six small target squares labelled R,
        Mg, B, Cy, G and Yl, and one white dot at the centre. A full width
        Inspector row shows four wheels, Position as a crosshair wheel with
        a centred puck and X 960 Y 540, Scale and Opacity as full white
        rings reading 100 percent, and Cross dissolve as a ring of 24 ticks
        with 12 lit reading 12 frames, each with a short note. A full width
        Media strip shows five numbered thumbnail cards with an image or
        bars glyph, the file name and duration with V or A. A thin Timeline
        panel last has 18px lanes on a faint graticule, grey clips with a
        grey edge, the selected title clip filled light grey with a diamond,
        an amber marker triangle with a dashed line and a white playhead
        with an up triangle and 18. At phone width only the viewer and the
        timeline remain.
    spacing: An 8px unit with 12px gaps between panels and 14px panel padding.
    density: Medium high. Scopes, picture, four wheels, a thumbnail strip and a thin timeline.
    corners: 8px panels, 6px buttons and cards, round transport buttons and wheels.
    borders: 1px #383838 panel edges and 1px #8a8a8a clip edges. Scopes sit borderless on black.
    shadows: A soft drop shadow under each wheel only, and a 6px grey surround on the picture.
    icons:
        Filled transport glyphs in round buttons. Wheels and rings show
        state by shape, always with the written value beneath. A diamond
        marks the selected clip, a down triangle the marker.
    focus: A 2px amber outline offset 2px, the only warm colour on the screen.
    tone: Technical and calm, such as Waveform luma, Puck centred and 12 of 24 ticks.
